---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'Flipside Privacy Policy | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'How Flipside for iPhone handles your photos, camera, microphone and motion. Everything is processed on your device; nothing is uploaded or collected.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Flipside', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/flipside-ios/` },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Flipside Privacy Policy',
    url: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/flipside-ios/`,
    description,
    dateModified: '2026-10-18',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Precision Solutions Tech', url: `${SITE}/` },
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/legal/privacy/flipside-ios/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li>Flipside</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Flipside Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: October 18, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Flipside</strong> (“we”, “us”) handles information
        when you use the Flipside app for iPhone (the “App”), published by
        <strong>Precision Solutions Tech</strong>, operated by <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summary">Short version</h2>
      <p>
        Flipside works <strong>entirely on your device</strong>. Your camera, your photos, your voice
        and everything the App measures stay on your iPhone. We collect no data, operate no account
        system, and run no servers that receive anything from the App. The App makes no network
        requests of its own, and it never asks for your location.
      </p>

      <h2 id="camera">Camera</h2>
      <p>
        The App uses the camera to coach you into the shot: it finds faces, people, hands (for the
        raised-palm shutter) and pets, and measures framing and light in the live picture, on your
        device. Live frames are analysed and discarded; they are not stored or sent anywhere. Only the
        photos you take are kept, and only while you use them in the App, until you save or share them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="microphone">Microphone and speech recognition (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        Only if you turn on “Say cheese”, the App listens for words like “cheese” or “take it” while the
        camera screen is open. Recognition runs <strong>on your iPhone only</strong>: the App requires
        on-device recognition and does not use it on iPhones that can’t do that, so your voice is never
        sent to Apple or to us. Nothing is recorded or kept.
      </p>

      <h2 id="motion">Motion</h2>
      <p>
        The App reads the motion sensor while the camera is open, to tell a phone in your hand from one
        on a stand and to take the photo at the steadiest moment. These readings are used on the spot
        and not stored.
      </p>

      <h2 id="photos">Photos</h2>
      <p>
        When you save a photo, the App asks for permission to <em>add</em> items to your Photos
        library. It cannot see or read your library. Saved and shared photos are newly encoded by the
        App and carry no location information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="processing">What the App processes on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Faces, bodies, hands and pets, head pose and eye openness, to coach, choose the best photo and fix blinks</li>
        <li>A person outline, for background blur and jump combos</li>
        <li>Scene type and light, to choose camera settings</li>
        <li>Your settings: voice output, timer, shooting style, hands-free options</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of this is used to identify you, and none of it leaves your device. Spoken directions use
        Apple’s on-device speech.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
      <p>
        The App is not directed to children and asks no one for personal information. Photos of
        anyone, of any age, are handled the same way: on your device, never collected by us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sharing">Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        When you share a photo or video (AirDrop, Messages, Mail, social apps), iOS sends it where you
        choose, and that service’s own privacy policy applies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The App contains <strong>no analytics SDKs, no advertising SDKs, and no third-party
        trackers</strong>. We do not profile you, and we do not sell or share personal information. If
        that ever changes, this policy will be updated before the change ships.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We hold no data from the App. Photos you save are yours to keep or delete. If you contact
        support, we keep your message as long as needed to help you.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/ios-apps/flipside/">Flipside</a>
        ·
        <a href="/ios-apps/flipside/support/">Support</a>
        ·
        <a href="/legal/privacy/">Company privacy policy</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
